# Review ownership: path pattern, then the teams whose approval is required.
#
# @phanlaw/platform is the organisation's default owner; @phanlaw/techlead is added where a wrong
# change is expensive and quiet. Both teams hold write access, which GitHub requires before a team
# can own code.

*                      @phanlaw/platform

# A token change reaches every surface, and the contrast tests are what stand between a palette
# edit and a screen an inspector cannot read in daylight.
/packages/tokens/      @phanlaw/platform @phanlaw/techlead

# The null-money rule and the four-state contract are correctness rules that look like styling.
/packages/formatting/  @phanlaw/platform @phanlaw/techlead
/packages/ui/          @phanlaw/platform @phanlaw/techlead

/.github/              @phanlaw/platform @phanlaw/techlead
